{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "zebra_puzzle:fe37c4db2b25d85eb28bc39dc6c978c002216c9e26227d7a9389abad0dd230f0", "sample_idx": 1, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "We are told there are two people in a line, numbered 1 (left) and 2 (right). Each has unique values for:\n\n- Movie-Genre: crime, animation  \n- Pet: ferret, lizard  \n- Transport: tram, jet-ski  \n\nEach attribute value is used exactly once (since each person has a unique value for each attribute, and there are two people).\n\nWe are given two clues:\n\n1. **The person who watches animation is on the immediate right of the person who has a ferret.**  \n   → So, ferret must be on the left (position 1), and animation must be on the right (position 2).  \n   Because there are only two positions, \"immediate right\" only makes sense if ferret is in 1 and animation in 2.\n\n   So:  \n   - Position 1: Pet = ferret  \n   - Position 2: Movie-Genre = animation  \n\n   Therefore, since animation is in position 2, the other movie genre (crime) must be in position 1.\n\n   So now we have:  \n   - Position 1: Pet = ferret, Movie = crime  \n   - Position 2: Movie = animation, Pet = lizard (only one left)\n\n2. **The person who watches crime is on the immediate left or immediate right of the person who travels by jet-ski.**  \n   → So crime and jet-ski are adjacent. Since there are only two people, they are always adjacent. So this clue just tells us that the person who watches crime is next to the person who uses jet-ski — which is always true in a 2-person line. So this doesn’t add new positional constraint, but tells us that **crime and jet-ski are not on the same person**? Wait — no, it says \"the person who watches crime is on the immediate left or right of the person who travels by jet-ski\" — meaning they are **different people**.\n\n   So: crime and jet-ski are on different people.\n\n   We already have:  \n   - Position 1: Movie = crime  \n   - Position 2: Movie = animation  \n\n   So jet-ski cannot be on position 1 (because then crime and jet-ski would be on same person, violating the clue).  \n   Therefore, jet-ski must be on position 2.  \n   Then, tram must be on position 1.\n\n   Let’s summarize:\n\n   **Position 1:**  \n   - Movie: crime  \n   - Pet: ferret  \n   - Transport: tram  \n\n   **Position 2:**  \n   - Movie: animation  \n   - Pet: lizard  \n   - Transport: jet-ski  \n\n   Now let’s verify both clues:\n\n   1. Animation is immediately right of ferret → ferret is in 1, animation in 2 → ✅  \n   2. Crime is adjacent to jet-ski → crime in 1, jet-ski in 2 → adjacent → ✅  \n\n   All constraints satisfied.\n\n   Now answer the questions:\n\n   - **What is the movie genre of the person who has a ferret?**  \n     → Person with ferret is in position 1 → movie genre = crime  \n\n   - **What movie genre does the person in position 2 watch?**  \n     → animation  \n\n   - **What transport does the person in position 2 use?**  \n     → jet-ski  \n\n   - **What transport does the person who has a ferret use?**  \n     → person with ferret is in position 1 → transport = tram  \n\n   So answers in order:  \n   1. crime  \n   2. animation  \n   3. jet-ski  \n   4. tram  \n\nFinal answer: <solution>crime, animation, jet-ski, tram</solution>", "logprobs": [{"token": "We", "logprob": -0.04858812317252159}, {"token": " are", "logprob": -0.07899197936058044}, {"token": " told", "logprob": -0.8259410858154297}, {"token": " there", "logprob": -0.08320390433073044}, {"token": " are", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " two", "logprob": -0.319649875164032}, {"token": " people", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.003513831179589033}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0005155664402991533}, {"token": " line", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0031874587293714285}, {"token": " numbered", "logprob": -0.029127096757292747}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.031151091679930687}, {"token": "1", "lo